然后他又说，用我五岁能听懂的方式解释给我听。

319
00:13:32.500 --> 00:13:32.940
I know.
我知道。

320
00:13:33.940 --> 00:13:37.760
So Oscar does this great lemonade stand analogy.
所以奥斯卡用了那个很棒的柠檬水摊的类比。

321
00:13:38.680 --> 00:13:40.600
Michael seems like he's getting it.
迈克尔看起来好像听懂了。

322
00:13:41.080 --> 00:13:44.560
Ultimately, in the end, we're not sure he totally got it.
但最终，我们不确定他是否完全理解了。

323
00:13:45.260 --> 00:13:50.820
But Oscar says, you need to spend this money today and you should really spend it on a new
不过奥斯卡说，你今天必须把这笔钱花掉，而且你真的应该把它花在买一台新

324
00:13:50.820 --> 00:13:52.760
copier because we need it.
复印机上，因为我们需要它。

325
00:13:52.880 --> 00:13:54.260
We desperately need it.
我们非常需要它。

326
00:13:54.520 --> 00:13:57.960
We had a fan question from Lauren Kay.
我们收到了劳伦·凯的一个粉丝提问。

327
00:13:58.600 --> 00:14:03.900
When Oscar is explaining the surplus to Michael and Michael says, explain it to me like I'm five.
当奥斯卡向迈克尔解释盈余，而迈克尔说，用我五岁能听懂的方式解释给我听时。

328
00:14:03.900 --> 00:14:08.220
There's this great line when Oscar says, then next summer.
奥斯卡说了句很棒的台词，他说，那明年夏天。

329
00:14:08.400 --> 00:14:10.940
And Michael says, I'll be six.
然后迈克尔说，我就六岁了。

330
00:14:11.520 --> 00:14:13.760
That made me laugh so hard.
那段让我笑得好厉害。

331
00:14:13.940 --> 00:14:15.100
So hard.
笑得不行。

332
00:14:15.820 --> 00:14:19.520
Lauren wanted to know, was that scripted or was it improvised?
劳伦想知道，那是剧本写的还是即兴发挥的？

333
00:14:19.640 --> 00:14:21.340
It was scripted.
那是剧本写的。

334
00:14:21.400 --> 00:14:21.620
Yeah.
没错。

335
00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:22.580
That beat.
那个节奏。

336
00:14:23.240 --> 00:14:24.820
Steve threw it away so perfectly.
史蒂夫抛梗抛得太完美了。

337
00:14:25.100 --> 00:14:26.040
It was so cute.
太可爱了。

338
00:14:26.200 --> 00:14:27.360
It was so innocent.
太天真无邪了。

339
00:14:27.820 --> 00:14:28.220
I know.
我知道。

340
00:14:28.760 --> 00:14:29.720
Oh, Michael.
噢，迈克尔。

341
00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:31.220
Well, he's very excited.
嗯，他非常兴奋。

342
00:14:31.220 --> 00:14:33.280
He knows it's something good, right?
他知道这是件好事，对吧？

343
00:14:33.620 --> 00:14:35.420
He grasped at least that.
他至少抓住了这一点。

344
00:14:35.580 --> 00:14:37.680
And he's going to announce to the whole bullpen.
他打算向整个办公区宣布。

345
00:14:37.840 --> 00:14:38.320
Yes.
是的。

346
00:14:38.520 --> 00:14:39.600
They've got a surplus.
他们有盈余了。

347
00:14:40.440 --> 00:14:43.080
And he thinks maybe we'll get a new copier.
而且他觉得也许我们能买台新复印机。

348
00:14:43.240 --> 00:14:44.080
And Pam's like, no, no, no.
帕姆却说，不，不，不。

349
00:14:44.220 --> 00:14:44.740
Wait, wait.
等等，等等。

350
00:14:44.840 --> 00:14:45.200
Hold up.
先别急。

351
00:14:45.360 --> 00:14:46.540
We need new chairs.
我们需要新椅子。

352
00:14:46.820 --> 00:14:47.180
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

353
00:14:47.760 --> 00:14:54.420
Toby feels like they really need a good air quality inspection for some of the silent killers.
托比觉得他们真的需要做一次空气质量检查，以防那些无声杀手。

354
00:14:54.620 --> 00:14:55.480
Here's Toby again.
托比又来了。

355
00:14:55.480 --> 00:14:57.220
He's worried about the radon gas.
他担心氡气。

356
00:14:57.220 --> 00:14:59.080
He's worried about the asbestos.
他担心石棉。

357
00:14:59.080 --> 00:15:02.540
This is the runner that the writers loved for Toby.
这是编剧们为托比设计的桥段。

358
00:15:03.560 --> 00:15:08.960
And this is the scene where we realize that Jim is not team chairs.
这一幕我们意识到吉姆并不支持买椅子。

359
00:15:09.560 --> 00:15:10.120
Mm-mm.
嗯嗯。

360
00:15:10.340 --> 00:15:11.520
He wants a copier.
他想要一台复印机。

361
00:15:11.720 --> 00:15:15.200
It really made me laugh hard when Creed goes, the ball's on you, man.
克里德说“球在你那儿，伙计”的时候，我真的笑得很大声。

362
00:15:16.400 --> 00:15:18.740
Creed's delivery was so good.
克里德的台词功底太好了。

363
00:15:19.200 --> 00:15:22.080
And Jenna, there was a Pam talking head that would have gone here.
还有珍娜，这里原本有一段帕姆的采访镜头。

364
00:15:22.420 --> 00:15:23.940
And it's about her chair.
是关于她椅子的。

365
00:15:24.100 --> 00:15:26.180
And you delivered it from reception.
而且你是从前台那里录的。

366
00:15:26.180 --> 00:15:28.120
It's a talking head from reception.
那是从前台录的采访。

367
00:15:28.120 --> 00:15:29.320
In my chair.
在我的椅子上。

368
00:15:29.960 --> 00:15:31.480
Standing next to your chair.
站在你的椅子旁边。

369
00:15:32.040 --> 00:15:33.220
Oh, what is it?
噢，那是什么？

370
00:15:33.440 --> 00:15:34.280
Sam, play it.
萨姆，播放一下。

371
00:15:34.920 --> 00:15:36.920
This is the chair that was here when I was hired.
这把椅子是我入职时就在这儿的。

372
00:15:37.620 --> 00:15:40.000
It was crappy then, and it's even worse now.
那时候就很烂了，现在更糟。

373
00:15:40.720 --> 00:15:43.740
To give myself a break, sometimes I go outside and sit on the ground.
为了让自己喘口气，我有时会去外面坐在地上。

374
00:15:44.960 --> 00:15:45.380
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

375
00:15:45.380 --> 00:15:46.420
I remember that now.
我现在想起来了。

376
00:15:46.660 --> 00:15:48.500
That's how bad that chair is.
那把椅子烂到这种程度。

377
00:15:49.480 --> 00:15:51.640
I thought Pam made a really strong argument.
我觉得帕姆的论点非常有说服力。

378
00:15:51.980 --> 00:15:56.340
She made me want to be team chair because she was like, I make the copies.
她让我想要支持买椅子，因为她说，复印是我在做。

379
00:15:56.640 --> 00:15:58.520
I'm the one that has to deal with the copier.
是我在处理复印机的事。

380
00:15:58.760 --> 00:16:01.420
That should tell you how bad these chairs are.
这足以说明这些椅子有多烂了。

381
00:16:01.820 --> 00:16:06.060
Well, and also, everyone would get a new chair, right?
嗯，而且每个人都能换把新椅子，对吧？

382
00:16:06.060 --> 00:16:08.940
So, it really is something for everyone.
所以这确实是惠及所有人的事。

383
00:16:09.500 --> 00:16:13.940
But the other thing I thought was just, what about the copier in the annex?
但我当时想的另一件事是，那附楼里的复印机呢？

384
00:16:15.320 --> 00:16:16.920
There's another copier.
还有另一台复印机。

385
00:16:17.100 --> 00:16:18.900
No one wants to walk to the annex.
没人想走到附楼去。

386
00:16:19.080 --> 00:16:20.200
It's icky back there.
那儿很恶心。

387
00:16:20.500 --> 00:16:22.120
Well, then they should swap them.
那他们应该换一下。

388
00:16:22.580 --> 00:16:23.340
I know.
我知道。

389
00:16:23.540 --> 00:16:25.620
Maybe Kelly needs to make a lot of copies.
也许凯莉需要复印很多东西。

390
00:16:25.900 --> 00:16:27.720
It feels like there's a simple solution.
感觉这有个简单的解决方案。

391
00:16:27.980 --> 00:16:29.200
To the copier problem.
针对复印机的问题。

392
00:16:29.400 --> 00:16:29.450
To the copier.
针对复印机。

393
00:16:29.520 --> 00:16:30.620
No one's realizing.
没人意识到这一点。

394
00:16:31.280 --> 00:16:35.320
Well, Michael's going to digest all of their ideas and see what comes out the other end.
嗯，迈克尔会消化他们所有的想法，看看最后会得出什么结论。

395
00:16:36.200 --> 00:16:42.140
Coming up at 3 minutes 56 seconds is a scene, Jenna, that I didn't think I was going to get through.
在3分56秒处有一个场景，珍娜，我以为我演不下去。

396
00:16:42.360 --> 00:16:45.160
I didn't think we would have any usable takes.
我以为我们拍不出任何可用的镜头。

397
00:16:45.400 --> 00:16:51.500
Last week, you talked about that clown painting on the wall in Jim's parents' house that you guys could not get through it.
上周，你提到了吉姆父母家墙上那幅小丑画，你们当时怎么也演不下去。

398
00:16:51.540 --> 00:16:52.000
You were laughing.
你们一直在笑。

399
00:16:52.240 --> 00:16:52.500
Yes.
是的。

400
00:16:52.700 --> 00:16:58.660
This scene with Dwight giving directions to Andy and Angela, that was it for me.
德怀特给安迪和安吉拉指路的那场戏，对我来说就是那样。

401
00:16:58.660 --> 00:17:01.920
Ed and I, we could not get through it.
我和埃德，我们根本演不下去。

402
00:17:02.160 --> 00:17:04.160
Like, truly, we could not stop laughing.
真的，我们根本停不下来笑。

403
00:17:04.440 --> 00:17:07.440
It's in the bloopers, and I think we've got to hear it.
花絮里有这段，我觉得我们得听听。

404
00:17:07.620 --> 00:17:14.160
You know, lady, last week, I looked at the bloopers to see if I could find any clown painting outtakes.
你知道吗，女士，上周我看了花絮，想看看能不能找到小丑画的废弃镜头。

405
00:17:14.280 --> 00:17:14.440
Yeah.
是啊。

406
00:17:14.540 --> 00:17:16.840
I couldn't find them, but I did see this.
我没找到那些，但我看到了这个。

407
00:17:16.980 --> 00:17:17.860
It is so good.
太棒了。

408
00:17:19.280 --> 00:17:24.700
Just, I feel like some of these directions to Shrewd Farms are a little weird.
我只是觉得去精明农场的这些指引有点奇怪。

409
00:17:25.300 --> 00:17:30.200
I mean, like, 156 paces from the light red mailbox, make a left.
我是说，比如，从浅红色邮箱走156步，然后左转。

410
00:17:31.300 --> 00:17:38.120
Walk until you hear the beehive, and make a right.
一直走到听到蜂巢的声音，然后右转。

411
00:17:38.340 --> 00:17:42.960
If you are attacked by territorial crows...
如果你遭到领地意识强的乌鸦攻击……

412
00:17:42.960 --> 00:17:46.640
I have, this is a really, he's...
我有，这真的是，他……

413
00:17:46.640 --> 00:17:50.120
If you smell bear pee, turn the other way.
如果你闻到熊尿味，就往反方向走。

414
00:17:50.860 --> 00:17:51.460
I...
我……

415
00:17:53.980 --> 00:17:57.060
If you smell bear pee at any point, abort.
如果你在任何时候闻到熊尿味，立刻撤退。

416
00:17:57.380 --> 00:17:59.160
Wait in your car for further instructions.
在车里等待进一步指示。

417
00:17:59.160 --> 00:18:00.420
What's the problem exactly?
到底有什么问题？

418
00:18:04.990 --> 00:18:09.950
The other thing that's so great about this blooper is that you're hearing all those candy bag alt directions.
这个花絮最棒的另一点是，你听到了所有那些糖果袋的备选指引。

419
00:18:10.350 --> 00:18:17.890
Yes, because in the script, the only directions were 156 paces from the light red mailbox, and then the one about the bear.
没错，因为剧本里原本的指引只有从浅红色邮箱走156步，还有关于熊的那条。

420
00:18:18.130 --> 00:18:20.390
All the rest are candy bag alts.
剩下的全是糖果袋的备选台词。

421
00:18:20.550 --> 00:18:24.590
So were they just, because in the clip, you can see that Ed is reading.
所以他们当时是……因为在片段里，你可以看到埃德在读。

422
00:18:24.910 --> 00:18:28.070
Were they just handing him pieces of paper with, like, funny directions?
他们是直接递给他写着搞笑指引的纸条吗？

423
00:18:28.310 --> 00:18:29.290
They literally did.
他们真的是这么做的。

424
00:18:29.290 --> 00:18:34.810
They handed him a whole paper that were extra directions, and that's why he was like, I almost had it.
他们递给他整整一张纸，上面全是额外的指引，所以他才会说，我差点就演成了。

425
00:18:35.870 --> 00:18:39.630
And if you guys watch the bloopers, you'll see that I'm sniffling.
如果你们看花絮，就会发现我在吸鼻子。

426
00:18:39.810 --> 00:18:48.990
I am sniffling because it was so cold on set that day that my nose was running, and I had a tissue in my hand that I was hiding under the table.
我在吸鼻子是因为那天片场太冷了，我流鼻涕了，我手里藏着一张纸巾在桌子底下。

427
00:18:49.170 --> 00:18:50.670
It was that cold.
当时就是那么冷。

428
00:18:50.870 --> 00:18:53.950
That used to happen to me all the time, my nose would run on set.
我以前也经常这样，在片场流鼻涕。

429
00:18:54.130 --> 00:18:54.570
I know.
我知道。

430
00:18:54.810 --> 00:18:58.670
I had my sneezing from the allergies and the runny nose from the cold.
我当时既有过敏引起的打喷嚏，又有天冷引起的流鼻涕。

431
00:18:58.670 --> 00:19:03.250
Well, I rewatched the scene, and all I can see is me sniffling and trying not to laugh.
好吧，我重看了那场戏，我只能看到自己在吸鼻子，还努力忍住不笑。

432
00:19:04.490 --> 00:19:06.010
Well, you laughed a lot.
嗯，你笑了很多次。

433
00:19:06.190 --> 00:19:06.590
I did.
确实。

434
00:19:07.210 --> 00:19:09.470
Well, Jenna, we had a fan question about this scene.
好吧，珍娜，我们有个关于这场戏的粉丝提问。

435
00:19:09.690 --> 00:19:10.610
Allie Jo H.
艾莉·乔·H.

436
00:19:10.770 --> 00:19:11.790
wrote in and said,
来信说，

437
00:19:11.950 --> 00:19:18.350
When Angela and Andy are talking to Dwight, Andy says something about a three-way, and it looks like Dwight mouths something to Angela.
当安吉拉和安迪跟德怀特说话时，安迪提到了三人行，看起来德怀特对着安吉拉说了什么。

438
00:19:18.510 --> 00:19:20.090
Do you remember what he said?
你还记得他说了什么吗？

439
00:19:20.090 --> 00:19:24.450
I can tell you, in the script, Rain had this stage direction.
我可以告诉你，在剧本里，雷恩有这样的舞台提示。

440
00:19:24.870 --> 00:19:29.750
It says, Dwight rolls his eyes to Angela like, ugh, check out the dummy.
上面写着，德怀特对安吉拉翻了个白眼，好像在说，呃，看看这个傻瓜。

441
00:19:29.970 --> 00:19:32.250
And Angela doesn't give him anything.
而安吉拉没给他任何回应。

442
00:19:32.850 --> 00:19:38.210
So I think Rain was sort of mocking Andy in that moment, like looking at me like, ugh, this guy.
所以我认为雷恩当时是在嘲笑安迪，看着我好像在说，呃，这家伙。

443
00:19:38.750 --> 00:19:41.170
Coming up, we have a scene that was really, really fun for me.
接下来，我们要看一场对我来说非常非常有趣的戏。

444
00:19:41.330 --> 00:19:47.670
It's the scene in the kitchen between Pam and Jim, where Pam is kind of low-key threatening Jim.
就是帕姆和吉姆在厨房的那场戏，帕姆在低调地威胁吉姆。

445
00:19:47.930 --> 00:19:48.390
Yeah.
是啊。

446
00:19:48.730 --> 00:19:49.470
To be on her side.
要站在她那边。

447
00:19:49.490 --> 00:19:50.530
Not low-key.
不是低调。

448
00:19:50.930 --> 00:19:51.550
Full-key?
是高调？

449
00:19:51.710 --> 00:19:52.570
Is that an expression?
那是个表达方式吗？

450
00:19:53.870 --> 00:19:55.950
We had a fan question from Jessica Kay.
我们收到了杰西卡·凯的一个粉丝提问。

451
00:19:56.110 --> 00:20:01.630
She would very much like us to discuss Pam's you're on dangerous ground moment, saying, quote,
她非常希望我们讨论一下帕姆那个“你现在很危险”的瞬间，引用她的话说，

452
00:20:01.630 --> 00:20:03.490
I was like, damn, Jenna.
我当时心想，天哪，珍娜。

453
00:20:05.830 --> 00:20:10.870
Well, Jessica, we came up with this little moment while we rehearsed the scene.
嗯，杰西卡，我们在排练这场戏时想出了这个小细节。

454
00:20:10.910 --> 00:20:20.330
So this idea of Pam going over to Jim and going in for a kiss but then pulling back, that was something that we did in rehearsal.
所以帕姆走向吉姆并试图亲吻他，但随后又退缩的这个点子，是我们排练时加进去的。

455
00:20:20.650 --> 00:20:24.390
It was not in the script, and we just were so tickled.
剧本里原本没有，我们当时觉得特别有意思。

456
00:20:24.390 --> 00:20:32.430
You know those moments when you're rehearsing a scene or you're doing a scene and you come up with this idea that just opens it up in this new way?
你知道那种感觉吗？当你排练或表演一场戏时，突然冒出一个点子，让整场戏有了全新的展开？

457
00:20:32.590 --> 00:20:33.590
It's so fun.
那真的太有趣了。

458
00:20:33.590 --> 00:20:41.370
And it's so fun to see everyone else realize it, too, because I have to imagine that when Paul Feig saw it, he was like, oh, yes, you have to do that.
看到其他人也意识到这一点也很有趣，因为我猜保罗·费格看到的时候肯定会说，噢，没错，你们一定要这么演。

459
00:20:41.690 --> 00:20:43.450
Yeah, it was really, really cool.
没错，那真的非常非常酷。

460
00:20:43.650 --> 00:20:46.190
And then we knew we shot this scene firSt.
而且我们当时就知道这场戏要先拍。

461
00:20:46.330 --> 00:20:50.190
We were going to mirror it in the tag at the end with Jim.
我们打算在结尾的彩蛋里用吉姆的戏来呼应它。

462
00:20:50.550 --> 00:20:51.610
Oh, it's so good.
噢，那太棒了。

463
00:20:51.610 --> 00:20:55.510
And I love Jim's talking head after where he was like, oh, spooky.
我特别喜欢吉姆之后对着镜头的采访，他说，噢，真诡异。

464
00:20:56.330 --> 00:20:58.730
You guys were about to head out to Shroop FarMs.
你们当时正准备出发去施鲁特农场。

465
00:20:59.010 --> 00:21:00.870
There was a deleted driving scene.
有一段被删减的开车戏。

466
