Andy continues to chew and then swallows the bite.
安迪继续咀嚼，然后咽下了那一口。

1257
00:54:57.280 --> 00:55:00.200
Angela wipes her mouth and hears the speech.
安吉拉擦了擦嘴，听着演讲。

1258
00:55:00.720 --> 00:55:04.360
I would marry you during an earthquake in the middle of a tornado.
就算是在龙卷风中心的地震中，我也愿意娶你。

1259
00:55:04.620 --> 00:55:08.280
I would marry you in the front row of an Elton John concert.
就算是在埃尔顿·约翰演唱会的第一排，我也愿意娶你。

1260
00:55:08.560 --> 00:55:11.020
I don't care how terrible a place it is.
我不在乎那地方有多糟糕。

1261
00:55:11.160 --> 00:55:12.760
I just want to be with you.
我只想和你在一起。

1262
00:55:13.300 --> 00:55:15.680
Now, I have a legal matter to clear up.
现在，我有一件法律事务要处理一下。

1263
00:55:15.680 --> 00:55:18.660
I'm not an Elton John fan.
我不是埃尔顿·约翰的粉丝。

1264
00:55:19.500 --> 00:55:19.900
Clearly.
显而易见。

1265
00:55:20.400 --> 00:55:21.200
Clearly not.
显然不是。

1266
00:55:22.420 --> 00:55:24.600
But yeah, so I had that speech I had to do.
但没错，我当时确实得做那个演讲。

1267
00:55:24.800 --> 00:55:28.140
And they gave me a few alts, you know, and I was really nervous.
他们给了我几个备选方案，你知道的，我当时真的很紧张。

1268
00:55:28.140 --> 00:55:31.520
But all that made it in was now I have a legal matter to clear up.
但最终保留下来的只有“现在我有一件法律事务要处理一下”。

1269
00:55:31.640 --> 00:55:34.920
And I actually think that was a good edit because the kiss was enough.
我其实觉得那是个不错的剪辑，因为那个吻已经足够了。

1270
00:55:35.080 --> 00:55:35.260
Yeah.
没错。

1271
00:55:35.620 --> 00:55:35.800
Right.
对。

1272
00:55:35.940 --> 00:55:39.160
That was enough of like shoving it in Dwight's face.
那样在德怀特面前炫耀已经够了。

1273
00:55:39.320 --> 00:55:40.680
I didn't need to make this speech.
我没必要非得做这个演讲。

1274
00:55:41.020 --> 00:55:42.640
But yes, no tuna.
但没错，没有金枪鱼。

1275
00:55:43.100 --> 00:55:43.580
Thank you, Ed.
谢谢你，埃德。

1276
00:55:43.580 --> 00:55:49.680
Very different from a kiss with Rain, who actually was eating tuna in real life.
这和雷恩的吻非常不同，他在现实生活中真的在吃金枪鱼。

1277
00:55:49.960 --> 00:55:52.740
Backstage for no reason at all.
在后台，毫无理由地。

1278
00:55:52.860 --> 00:55:53.660
Knowing he has.
明知他有。

1279
00:55:53.740 --> 00:55:54.420
Before a kissing scene.
在吻戏之前。

1280
00:55:54.680 --> 00:56:00.080
Yes, that or drinking coffee while eating like an everything bagel that had onions on it.
是的，要么就是喝着咖啡，同时吃着那种加了洋葱的全料贝果。

1281
00:56:00.240 --> 00:56:00.420
Yeah.
是啊。

1282
00:56:00.940 --> 00:56:01.220
Different.
不同。

1283
00:56:01.580 --> 00:56:02.120
Very different.
非常不同。

1284
00:56:02.320 --> 00:56:02.800
Approaches.
方式。

1285
00:56:05.860 --> 00:56:10.020
This whole copier chair thing is going to wrap up.
关于复印机和椅子的整件事就要结束了。

1286
00:56:10.160 --> 00:56:12.940
The employees are going to confront Michael in his office.
员工们要去办公室找迈克尔对质。

1287
00:56:12.940 --> 00:56:15.360
And he basically tells them, you know what?
他基本上告诉他们，你们知道吗？

1288
00:56:15.520 --> 00:56:16.540
You decide.
你们自己决定吧。

1289
00:56:16.780 --> 00:56:20.440
You all have to agree or else I'm taking the bonus.
你们所有人必须达成一致，否则我就拿走奖金。

1290
00:56:20.440 --> 00:56:23.700
Because he kind of thinks like there's no way that's going to happen, right?
因为他觉得这根本不可能发生，对吧？

1291
00:56:23.940 --> 00:56:25.660
Of course he thinks there's no way.
他当然觉得不可能。

1292
00:56:25.760 --> 00:56:26.920
He thinks he got them.
他以为他拿捏住他们了。

1293
00:56:26.920 --> 00:56:29.460
They very quickly decide to get the chairs.
他们很快就决定要椅子了。

1294
00:56:29.820 --> 00:56:31.740
He was like, son of a.
他当时就像是，该死的。

1295
00:56:31.960 --> 00:56:33.620
He actually says mother.
他其实说的是“妈的”。

1296
00:56:33.920 --> 00:56:34.700
Yeah, he does.
没错，他说了。

1297
00:56:34.980 --> 00:56:35.320
F.
F开头的那个词。

1298
00:56:36.100 --> 00:56:38.280
Was he putting sugar in his Diet Coke?
他是在往健怡可乐里加糖吗？

1299
00:56:38.360 --> 00:56:39.000
He was.
是的，他在加。

1300
00:56:39.200 --> 00:56:40.540
Yeah, he wanted to sweeten it.
没错，他想让它变甜一点。

1301
00:56:40.720 --> 00:56:41.500
Oh, my Lord.
天哪。

1302
00:56:43.200 --> 00:56:45.580
The whole thing kind of ends with Michael.
整件事最后是以迈克尔收尾的。

1303
00:56:45.640 --> 00:56:47.060
He has a talking head.
他有个单独采访。

1304
00:56:47.060 --> 00:56:48.460
He wants you to know what he learned.
他想让你知道他学到了什么。

1305
00:56:48.920 --> 00:56:49.800
What did he learn?
他学到了什么？

1306
00:56:50.020 --> 00:56:53.580
He learned that his team is faster at making a decision than he thought.
他学到他的团队做决定的速度比他想象的要快。

1307
00:56:54.040 --> 00:56:58.180
He also learned you should never buy a fur coat with a credit card until you actually
他还学到在真正有钱支付之前，

1308
00:56:58.180 --> 00:56:59.720
have the money to pay for it.
千万别用信用卡买皮草大衣。

1309
00:56:59.920 --> 00:57:01.900
Michael, why in the world are you buying a fur coat?
迈克尔，你到底为什么要买皮草大衣？

1310
00:57:02.040 --> 00:57:03.160
You're never going to wear it.
你根本不会穿它的。

1311
00:57:03.900 --> 00:57:05.240
It's ridiculous looking.
看起来太荒唐了。

1312
00:57:05.480 --> 00:57:05.920
Yes.
确实。

1313
00:57:06.160 --> 00:57:08.940
He's just like a kid that gets money and doesn't know what to do with it.
他就像个拿到钱却不知道该怎么花的孩子。

1314
00:57:09.040 --> 00:57:13.620
In his mind, that's, I don't know, fancy luxury or something.
在他看来，那是什么，高级奢侈品之类的吧。

1315
00:57:13.960 --> 00:57:15.580
Fancy people have those or something.
有钱人都有那种东西之类的。

1316
00:57:15.780 --> 00:57:16.460
I guess so.
我想是吧。

1317
00:57:16.640 --> 00:57:20.200
The third thing he learned is that people think it's cool to throw fake blood on you
他学到的第三件事是，人们觉得在你离开伯灵顿大衣工厂时，

1318
00:57:20.200 --> 00:57:22.220
as you leave Burlington Coat Factory.
往你身上泼假血很酷。

1319
00:57:22.940 --> 00:57:28.080
So he has a ruined fur coat that he bought on credit.
所以他现在有一件用信用卡买的、被毁了的皮草大衣。

1320
00:57:28.240 --> 00:57:28.960
That he can't afford.
而且他还买不起。

1321
00:57:29.400 --> 00:57:29.620
Yeah.
是啊。

1322
00:57:29.880 --> 00:57:31.080
That's how his day ended.
他的一天就是这样结束的。

1323
00:57:31.380 --> 00:57:31.560
Yeah.
是啊。

1324
00:57:33.160 --> 00:57:35.820
Jim and Pam's day is going to end with a truce.
吉姆和帕姆的一天将以休战告终。

1325
00:57:36.020 --> 00:57:38.560
But oh, can you make me three copies of this?
但是，噢，你能帮我复印三份这个吗？

1326
00:57:38.700 --> 00:57:39.360
I'm just kidding.
开个玩笑。

1327
00:57:39.360 --> 00:57:40.200
I need four.
我要四份。

1328
00:57:40.680 --> 00:57:42.200
Is this Jim sass?
这是吉姆式的调侃吗？

1329
00:57:42.380 --> 00:57:44.040
Oh, that's some Jim sass.
噢，那确实是吉姆式的调侃。

1330
00:57:44.280 --> 00:57:46.100
I have one final question for you.
我最后还有一个问题要问你。

1331
00:57:46.280 --> 00:57:46.560
Yes.
好的。

1332
00:57:46.980 --> 00:57:49.300
Would you be team copier or team chair?
你会选复印机派还是椅子派？

1333
00:57:50.020 --> 00:57:50.780
Team chair.
椅子派。

1334
00:57:51.320 --> 00:57:52.300
What would you be?
你会选什么？

1335
00:57:52.900 --> 00:57:53.480
Team chair.
椅子派。

1336
00:57:54.160 --> 00:57:54.360
Yeah.
是啊。

1337
00:57:54.680 --> 00:57:57.220
Team copier doesn't even make any sense to me, frankly.
坦白说，复印机派对我来说根本说不通。

1338
00:57:57.560 --> 00:58:00.120
I mean, I would just suffer through a crappy machine.
我的意思是，我宁愿忍受一台烂机器。

1339
00:58:00.120 --> 00:58:03.760
How many times have you worked in an office where either the fax machine, I know I'm a
你在办公室工作时，有多少次遇到过传真机——我知道我是个老古董了——

1340
00:58:03.760 --> 00:58:06.720
dinosaur, or the copier didn't work great.
或者复印机不好用的情况。

1341
00:58:06.840 --> 00:58:09.120
But a chair, that's like your tailbone.
但椅子，那可是关系到你的尾椎骨。

1342
00:58:09.240 --> 00:58:10.060
That's your spine.
那是你的脊椎。

1343
00:58:10.060 --> 00:58:11.000
That's your butt.
那是你的屁股。

1344
00:58:11.000 --> 00:58:12.900
Is anyone team copier?
有人选复印机派吗？

1345
00:58:13.000 --> 00:58:15.240
Can we put a poll in Office Ladies Pod today?
我们今天能在《办公室女士》播客里发起投票吗？

1346
00:58:15.600 --> 00:58:16.900
I'm so curious.
我太好奇了。

1347
00:58:17.340 --> 00:58:18.920
I'll put a poll and we'll see.
我会发起投票，然后我们来看看结果。

1348
00:58:19.140 --> 00:58:19.800
We want to see.
我们想看看。

1349
00:58:20.060 --> 00:58:23.040
Well, you guys, that was Spend the Surplus.
好了，各位，这就是《消耗盈余》那一集。

1350
00:58:23.520 --> 00:58:25.900
And also, Angela's birthday.
还有，安吉拉的生日。

1351
00:58:26.360 --> 00:58:26.900
Yay!
耶！

1352
00:58:27.240 --> 00:58:28.600
Whoop, whoop, whoo-hoo!
呜呼，呜呼，呜呼！

1353
00:58:29.360 --> 00:58:30.960
Yay, Angela.
耶，安吉拉。

1354
00:58:31.300 --> 00:58:31.600
Yay!
耶！

1355
00:58:31.800 --> 00:58:35.800
Next time I talk to you guys, I'll be American surveyed, 50 to 75.
下次我和你们通话时，我就已经完成美国人口普查了，50到75岁的那部分。

1356
00:58:36.120 --> 00:58:36.700
That'll be me.
那个人会是我。

1357
00:58:38.900 --> 00:58:40.140
See you next week.
下周见。

1358
00:58:40.160 --> 00:58:40.500
Bye!
再见！

1359
00:58:43.900 --> 00:58:45.900
Thank you for listening to Office Ladies.
感谢收听《办公室女士》。

